{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id317797285"}, "name":{"label":"DrowningInIt"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-05-11T21:27:13-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"2"}, "im:version":{"label":"4.4.8"}, "id":{"label":"14054991240"}, "title":{"label":"Decent, but barebones"}, "content":{"label":"The features that present in the unpaid use of the app are even less extensive than built-in apps for the calendar and your reminders in iOS. Literally the calendar app doesn’t charge you for the basic utilities that this app tries to present as premium and not baseline normal functioning of a digital planner of any kind. Example: you cannot set a recurring reminder. Unless you give them a subscription fee. Alarm clocks from 1982 had this ability, but here it is carved out of the UX in order to nickel and dime the user thru irritations & baffling inconveniences or omissions. Deleting this after I finish this in thinking. Tried to give it a fair shot. But this model of monetizing is egregious and also just straightforwardly stupid in its execution.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=1499198946&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
